        <item>
            <key> <string>description</string> </key>
            <value> <string>Delete a Python Script (or other object) from a portal_skins folder.\n
\n
    ⚠ DESTRUCTIVE: removes server-side code. There is no undo other than\n
    recreating the object.\n
\n
    USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - A script created for a one-off task should be cleaned up again.\n
    - You wrote a probe or bootstrap script with erp5_skin_write and are done.\n
    - You need to remove an object from any skin folder.\n
\n
    DO NOT USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - You want to delete a document in a module — use erp5_delete. That tool\n
      goes through Base_deleteObject and does NOT work on portal_skins: it\n
      reports success without removing anything.\n
    - You only want to change a script — use erp5_skin_write.\n
\n
    Any skin folder is accepted. Deleting from a folder other than \'custom\'\n
    removes an object owned by a business template: the instance then differs\n
    from its bt5 and a reinstall restores the object. That case is allowed but\n
    reported back in a \'warning\' key.\n
\n
    The deletion is confirmed by re-reading the folder afterwards, because\n
    manage_delObjects can return without error and still leave the object.\n
\n
    Returns JSON with: status, script_id, skin_folder, deleted, meta_type,\n
    and warning when the folder is not \'custom\'.\n
    </string> </value>
        </item>
